// transcribed from). Six board instances tile a 2x3 grid, one map per cell
// chosen by (row+col)%3, so no two horizontally- or vertically-adjacent boards
// (including across the tile's own repeat boundary) ever share a map.
// HEX_STROKE_PATH is every space's thin outline, across all six board instances.
// HEX_OCEAN_FILL_PATH / HEX_VOLCANIC_FILL_PATH: the same real board spaces'
// outlines again, split out by eligibility (all 12 ocean spaces per instance,
// regardless of whether they got an actual tile; all volcanic spaces) so they can
// be given a solid blue / brown fill, matching how the real board marks them.
// HEX_BORDER_PATH is each board instance's own outer silhouette (edges shared by
// two hexes cancel out, leaving just the perimeter), meant for a thicker stroke
// so adjacent boards read as distinct maps rather than one continuous mesh.
// HEX_BACKGROUND_STROKE_PATH is a plain connecting hex grid (no tiles, no
// resource icons) filling the space between/around the real boards so they
// don't sit in empty dark space — meant to be styled identically to
// HEX_STROKE_PATH so it reads as one continuous grid, not a separate backdrop.
